    "body": "### Problem\n\nAs in the title. See reproduction instructions below.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nDownload latest nightly:\n\n```\nrm -f nvim-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\ncurl -LO https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/download/nightly/nvim-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\nrm -rf nvim-linux-x86_64\ntar xzvf nvim-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\ncd nvim-linux-x86_64\n```\n\nRun in bash:\n\n```\nseq 1 286 > /tmp/test.txt\n./bin/nvim --clean /tmp/test.txt\n```\n\nThen in nvim:\n\n```\n:set hidden autoread noswapfile foldmethod=manual foldlevel=0 foldenable relativenumber | 262,283fold | call cursor(285, 1) | vnew | tabnew\n```\n\nIn another terminal:\n\n```\nsed -i '242,$d' /tmp/test.txt\n```\n\nIn nvim, run `:checktime` while still in the empty tab, then `gt`.\n\nSee nvim hangs and consumes 100% CPU. It may show things like `E315: ml_get: Invalid lnum: 285` first, press Escape.\nIf terminal has too few rows, it may \"merely\" show the `E315: ml_get: Invalid lnum: 285` without getting into an infinite loop.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo error seen, no infinite loop seen.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1868+gbe5167e21c\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nApparently yes. 9.2.283\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nxterm\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ndoesn't matter\n\n### Installation\n\ndownload nightly release",
